  "method_changes": [
    "Genuine erased object storage using native count header / fixed-stride slots / byte bitmap and block pointer table growth.",
    "Native function-pointer callbacks and context adapters; occupied self-set receives identical source and target raw pointers.",
    "New copies publish occupancy/count only after callback returns; failed construction retains allocated empty blocks.",
    "Unset, shared-slot assignment removal and whole-block destruction retain distinct native callback-visible count/occupancy timing.",
    "Stored destructor executes at Drop; exchange carries allocator, layout, state and callback identity.",
    "Legacy base iterator directly traverses raw blocks and retains capacity+blocksize exhaustion when scanning allocated blocks.",
    "Miri Drop-observation regression required shared Rc<UnsafeCell<State>> allocation; inline state was invalidated by Drop unique retag. Final test verifies observer pointer provenance."
  ],
  "remaining_partial_contracts": [
    "Typed SparseArray still uses its existing BTreeMap<Option<T>> implementation; delegation to this raw engine is not included.",
    "Rc/UnsafeCell erased storage is intentionally not Send/Sync. Typed SparseArray delegation needs explicit threading/ownership design so existing typed auto-traits do not silently regress.",
    "NCollection_SparseArrayBase::BasicIterator arbitrary container/value specialization and mutable shallow aliases remain unported.",
    "Native protected-state fields use unsafe raw state access; native private Block layout has a public unsafe Rust projection. Full compiler closure/cross-platform configuration proof remains pending.",
    "Allocator injection and context closures are Rust extensions; baseline native operations use the common allocator. Out-of-memory propagation currently uses panic rather than native Standard_OutOfMemory exception mapping.",
    "Callbacks must not perform reentrant mutations; destructor callbacks must not unwind. Native undefined alignment/invalid-index/overflow cases are not made parity claims.",
    "Detached iterator value/Index uses Option/zero instead of native undefined pointer access; exchange self-borrow is not directly expressible via its Rust mutable-reference signature."
  ],
